  "title": "How to Simplify Algebraic Expressions",
  "content": "<p><strong>Like terms</strong> have the same variable(s) raised to the same power. Collect them by adding or subtracting coefficients.</p><p>\\(3x\\) and \\(5x\\) are like terms. \\(3x\\) and \\(3x^2\\) are <em>not</em>.</p><p>When multiplying: multiply coefficients and add powers. When dividing: divide coefficients and subtract powers.</p>",
  "example": "<p><strong>Simplify</strong> \\(4x + 3y - 2x + 5y\\)</p><p>Group: \\((4x - 2x) + (3y + 5y) = 2x + 8y\\)</p>"
 },
